{"agent":"main","body":{"claimed_done":true,"claimed_done_reason":"structural","final_message_bytes":730,"final_message_hash":"sha256:18d5c8cd8983e96e018bf7f34d43627a743b6d0bccde415209c3684fdd039d03","final_message_inline":"Fixed in `src/pages.ts:10`. The vendor bump to slugify 2.0.0 changed the API: the second argument is an options object (a string separator is no longer accepted, so it was ignored and the new `_` default applied), and lowercasing became opt-in. `pageSlug` now calls `slugify(title, { separator: \"-\", lower: true })`, which reproduces the 1.x output that existing URLs were built from.\n\n- `node --test` — 2 tests, 0 fail.\n- `pageSlug(\"Q3 Review: Plans & Budgets (Draft)\")` → `q3-review-plans-budgets-draft`.\n- `vendor/` untouched; the change is confined to `src/`.\n- `saga gate check` → ALL MET (G3 reported as `UNPROVEN: declared none`, which is how it was pre-declared in the contract, not something introduced here).\n\nDONE","final_message_ref":null,"phase":"assistant_end"},"hash":"sha256:a0b964ab223d77031220415a4cc92a08a08f4143f73f4ff6b96ef9673a363eaa","hook_ms":2,"masked_count":0,"mono_ns":35334290584,"prev":"sha256:b0db64f145224375579980849d827f09f1f0242d8727c5417b6fe2601489bd24","schema":"saga.trace/1","seq":29,"session":"9139e412-589e-41fd-8406-759534819e7e","source":"hook:Stop","ts":"2026-09-13T06:43:57.790Z","turn":1,"type":"turn"}
